* NE555 precision timer: Ohmforge macromodel (original work, not a vendor
* model). Licence: CC-BY-SA-4.0, like the rest of parts/.
*
* Source: TI SLFS022K "xx555 Precision Timers" (revised March 2026).
* Standard SPICE primitives only (R, C, D, V, I, E, G, S), so ngspice runs
* it unchanged for validation. Typical values at 25 C, VCC 5 to 15 V.
*
* Ports: gnd trig out reset cont thres disch vcc (DIP-8 pins 1 to 8).
*
* What it models, and from where:
* - Divider: three 5 kOhm resistors VCC-CONT-lo-GND (6.2 Functional Block
*   Diagram, Figure 6-1), so CONT sits at 2/3 VCC open (5.5: 10 V typ at
*   15 V) and an external CONT moves both points: THRES compares with CONT,
*   TRIG with CONT / 2 (pin table 4-1: "TRIG < 1/2 CONT").
* - Comparators: ideal (switches with a 1 mV hysteresis band); 5.5 gives
*   10 V and 5 V typ at 15 V, exactly 2/3 and 1/3.
* - Latch (node q, 0 or 1 V): TRIG below CONT / 2 sets it, THRES above CONT
*   resets it, TRIG wins when both are active and RESET below 0.7 V (5.5
*   typ, 0.3 to 1 V) wins over both (Table 6-1). Hold switches keep the
*   state. q has no capacitor: a fast RC there rings under trapezoidal
*   integration at long steps and could flip the latch early, so the
*   output edges are instant (5.6: 100 ns typ, far below demo time scales).
* - Output: high = VCC - 0.9 V - 8 Ohm x I, low = 8 Ohm x I. The 8 Ohm and
*   0.9 V fit the 5.5 VOH table exactly (13.3 V at -100 mA, 12.5 V at
*   -200 mA, VCC = 15 V; 3.3 V at -100 mA, VCC = 5 V); 8 Ohm low gives
*   0.08 V at 10 mA and 0.4 V at 50 mA (5.5: 0.1 and 0.4 V typ). Above
*   about 60 mA the real low side leaves saturation (2 V typ at 100 mA);
*   this model does not (0.8 V), a known limit.
* - Discharge: 19 Ohm on (5.5: 0.15 V typ at 8 mA), 250 MOhm off (20 nA
*   typ off-state current at 5 V).
* - Pin currents (5.5): THRES draws 30 nA, TRIG sources 0.5 uA, RESET is
*   10 kOhm to 0.8 VCC (-0.4 mA at 0 V and +0.1 mA at VCC, VCC = 5 V).
* - Supply current (5.5, no load): output high 2 mA at 5 V and 9 mA at
*   15 V (a diode, 1.66 V and 1.58 kOhm, plus the 15 kOhm divider), and
*   1 mA more with the output low (3 and 10 mA typ).
* Timing checks in tests/ne555_datasheet.rs use the NE555 typical initial
* timing error (1 % monostable, 2.25 % astable) from SLFS022 revised
* February 1992, page 5, "operating characteristics" (dropped in rev K).
* VCC 4.5 to 16 V (5.3) is the recommended range; the model runs outside
* it but the figures above are only claimed inside.
* - Undervoltage lockout (an assumption: SLFS022K gives no UVLO or minimum
*   operating figure, only the 4.5 V minimum of 5.3). Below about 2.3 V a
*   bipolar 555's comparator and output stages have no headroom, so the
*   model holds the latch reset there (output low, discharge on) and lets it
*   go above 2.5 V rising (2.3 V falling): a Schmitt comparator whose
*   output (node en) lowers its own threshold by 0.2 V once released, so
*   a release holds even when the load it switches on pulls VCC down
*   within the same step, and no comparator decides anything while locked.
*   It senses VCC through a 10 us low-pass (buffered, so it draws nothing),
*   as a real comparator takes time to respond; on a current-limited
*   supply too weak for the load the chip hiccups in and out of lockout as
*   a real one does. Above 2.5 V
*   nothing changes (two 10 mOhm switches in the latch's set and reset
*   paths). Without it the comparators chatter at VCC near 0 during a cold
*   start (all their inputs within the 1 mV band) and the latch flips on
*   every Newton iteration.
.subckt ne555 gnd trig out reset cont thres disch vcc
* Divider (6.2).
R1 vcc cont 5k
R2 cont lo 5k
R3 lo gnd 5k
* Logic references (internal, relative to GND).
Vqh qh gnd 1
Vhalf half gnd 0.5
Vrst rstref gnd 0.7
* Latch: set by TRIG < CONT/2, reset by THRES > CONT, RESET pin first.
* The comparators reach q only while the lockout is released (en high).
Sset qs qh lo trig nesw
Suvs q qs en half neuven
Sthr qt gnd thres cont nesthr
Suvt q qt en half neuven
Srst q gnd rstref reset nesrst
* Undervoltage lockout: en goes high above 2.5 V and low below 2.3 V (its
* threshold is 2.5 V - 0.2 x en); while en is low the latch is held reset.
Euv uvbuf gnd vcc gnd 1
Ruv uvbuf uvs 10k
Cuv uvs gnd 1n
Vuvx uvx gnd 2.5
Euvth uvth uvx en gnd -0.2
Suven en qh uvs uvth neuvc
Ren en gnd 100k
Suvlo q gnd half en neuvlo on
Rqs qs gnd 1g
Rqt qt gnd 1g
Shi q qh q half nehold
Slo q gnd half q nehold on
* qn = 1 - q.
Eqn qn gnd qh q 1
* Output stage (5.5 VOH/VOL fit).
Voh vcc ohs 0.9
Sout1 ohs out q half neout
Sout0 out gnd qn half neout
* Discharge transistor (5.5).
Sdis disch gnd qn half nedis
* Pin bias (5.5).
Ithr thres gnd 30n
Dthr gnd thres nediode
Itrig gnd trig 0.5u
Dtrig trig vcc nediode
Ermid rmid gnd vcc gnd 0.8
Rrst reset rmid 10k
* Supply current (5.5).
Dq vcc qa nediode
Vq qa qb 1.66
Rq qb gnd 1.58k
Gq vcc gnd qn gnd 1m
.model nesw sw(vt=0 vh=1m ron=10 roff=1e12)
.model nesthr sw(vt=0 vh=1m ron=100 roff=1e12)
.model nesrst sw(vt=0 vh=1m ron=0.1 roff=1e12)
.model nehold sw(vt=0 vh=0.1 ron=10k roff=1e12)
.model neout sw(vt=0 vh=0.1 ron=8 roff=1e9)
.model nedis sw(vt=0 vh=0.1 ron=19 roff=250meg)
.model neuven sw(vt=0 vh=0.1 ron=10m roff=1e12)
.model neuvlo sw(vt=0 vh=0.1 ron=0.1 roff=1e12)
.model neuvc sw(vt=0 vh=1m ron=1k roff=1e12)
.model nediode d is=1e-14 n=1
.ends ne555
